  "limitations": [
    "Countywide candidate-vote comparisons are not ballots cast, distinct voters or evidence of wrongdoing. Different nominees, district maps, competition and incomplete current counting limit interpretation.",
    "2022 research county vectors retain exact MEDSL/upstream provenance and every source ID. One actual Gwinnett/CD7 named-write-in row supplies14 votes; no statewide total was allocated and no Fulton zero was created.",
    "Gwinnett unresolved write-ins9/CD6,11/CD7,70/CD9 are retained as unknown sourceReportingCategory with sourceNeedsReview; the county remains ineligible for party comparison. No validity or party assignment is inferred. Named LisaBabbage source label WRITE-IN is normalized Other.",
    "2026 direct official current county vectors replace the older registered snapshot only after full candidate-ID/name/party and separate whole-election summary reconciliation. All current records remain unofficial/provisional; reporting units do not establish certified or completed counting.",
    "Both full159-county inventories are matched to Census2024 roster. County compatibility uses retained substantial-change register; minor cartographic changes not independently adjudicated. District intersections can differ by year; no same-seat assertion.",
    "FEC full-name differences remain explicit, including Henry versus HarryC.HankJohnsonJr; same party/state/district/full family nickname and exact candidate totals support a control correspondence, not silent canonical renaming."
  ],
